!}

= The promises follow us into the ministries

The ministerial nameplates are barely fixed when Prime Minister **[+
prime_minister +]** summons the coalition leaders back to the table. A place
inside the **[+ government_name +]** has bought Lewica authority, but it has
also made every delay and concession part of our own record.

Our parliamentary leaders, **[+ government_burden_leaders +]**, send the same warning to
the cabinet and the party offices. Hospital staff, tenants, trade unionists,
families using public services and the equality movements did not vote for
better access to a coalition council. They expect something they can use.

Before six months pass, we must deliver in at least **two different fields**:
public health; housing and tenant security; labour rights; the social floor;
or material equality. Government Affairs cards and coalition disputes can put
those promises into effect. One explicitly marketising or anti-social
settlement, however, will stain the whole half-year even if other ministries
deliver.

- @entry_continue

@entry_continue
title: Accept the ministries—and start the clock
subtitle: Every Lewica minister and whip receives the same five commitments.

The list goes to our ministers, parliamentary whips and regional offices. For
the next six months, coalition communiqués will count for nothing unless a
nurse, tenant, worker, claimant or equality campaigner can point to the change.
The first review is already in the diary.

- @poland_event_queue: File the compact with the events desk

