= Six months in government — who can point to a change?

Prime Minister **[+ prime_minister +]** arrives at the coalition review with a
folder of cabinet announcements. Lewica's delegation brings a harsher ledger:
which promises can now be felt in a ward, a workplace, a rented home or a
public office?

The record contains **[+ government_burden_last_completed +] completed
fields; two were required**: [+ government_burden_last_goals +].

[? if government_burden_last_breached: Whatever else our ministers delivered,
the conservative settlement owns the verdict. Trade unionists, public-service
workers and Razem organisers can all say that Lewica used cabinet authority to
open the door it promised to hold shut. The half-year is lost.?]
[? if not government_burden_last_breached and government_burden_last_completed < 2:
There is no single betrayal for the leadership to disown—only too little that
survived the cabinet calendar. Local councillors are left defending meetings
and drafts while voters ask what changed. The half-year is lost.?]
[? if not government_burden_last_breached and government_burden_last_completed >= 2:
At least two constituencies leave the review with more than a promise. Our
coalition partners may share the ribbon-cutting, but **[+ government_burden_leaders +]** can
defend government as an instrument rather than an invitation to the room. The
half-year is won.?]

The verdict is public. None of its achievements can be counted a second time.

- @review_continue

@review_continue
title: Carry the verdict into another six months
subtitle: The old record remains; the five commitments begin again from zero.

The coalition secretary opens a clean page, but the party does not receive a
clean memory. Ministers must find two new constituencies to deliver for before
the next review, while every opposition speech will quote the record we have
just made.

- @poland_event_queue: Return the government record to the events desk

@health_market
# prose-audit: Grade B — The health minister, NFZ queue and public-service constituency anchor all three routes, with distinct coalition aftermaths; voice can still sharpen around alternate cabinets.
title: The coalition opens a private-health lane
subtitle: KO wants private capacity; Lewica must decide whether it is overflow, escape or surrender.
