= “Later” becomes a policy

Prime Minister **[+ prime_minister +]** wants the cabinet's next victories to
be judicial repair, EU milestones and reassurance for the Finance Ministry.
Labour Minister **[+ labor_minister +]** of **[+ labor_minister_party +]** comes
to the coalition council with benefit thresholds losing value and an
inspection service still waiting for enforceable deadlines.

The chancellery calls its request sequencing. Trade union organisers, social
workers and families caught above frozen thresholds call it the old ritual by
which a social chapter is praised, postponed and finally omitted. Lewica can
force money onto the table, exchange order for a date, or accept a promise no
minister will have to break because no minister has made it.

- @social_floor_now
- @social_labor_deadline
- @social_wait

@social_floor_now
title: Spend the reserve before inflation writes welfare policy
subtitle: Cost: 1 budget. Delivers the social floor now; the chancellery loses control of its sequence.
choose-if: budget >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Indexation requires one budget point.
on-arrival: budget -= 1; household_security += 5; workers_support += 3; government_delivery += 3; government_goal_welfare = 1; ko_relation -= 2; government_coalition_dissent += 4; fiscal_stress += 2; news_headline = "Benefit thresholds rise before another cabinet review"

The reserve goes into benefit thresholds before another month can erode them.
Local offices notify households of the new floor; the Finance Ministry
circulates the cost before the ink is dry. **[+ labor_minister +]** can show a
change rather than a calendar entry, while KO's managers record that Lewica
overruled the sequence in full view of the cabinet.

- @poland_event_queue: File the social settlement with the events desk

@social_labor_deadline
title: Yield the order, not the deadline: put inspection in statute
subtitle: Labour enforcement gets a binding date and welfare waits; the coalition keeps a workable sequence.
on-arrival: labor_credibility += 4; workers_support += 3; government_delivery += 2; government_goal_labor = 1; ko_relation += 1; p2050_relation += 2; government_coalition_dissent += 1; news_headline = "The coalition calendar acquires a binding labour-enforcement date"

Lewica lets the institutional bills go first only after the inspection
deadline is written into statute. Union lawyers receive a date they can defend
and employers receive one they must prepare for. Welfare groups still wait,
but the chancellery can no longer turn sequence into disappearance without
publicly breaking the bargain.

- @poland_event_queue: File the social settlement with the events desk

@social_wait
title: Give the chancellery its undated “later”
subtitle: Coalition peace now; the absent date breaches Lewica's entire six-month record.
on-arrival: ko_relation += 4; p2050_relation += 3; psl_relation += 2; government_coalition_dissent -= 5; labor_dissent += 5; progressives_dissent += 4; razem_dissent += 6; coalition_blur += 4; government_burden_breached = 1; news_headline = "Social reform leaves the cabinet calendar without a date"

No date appears in the minutes. The prime minister's staff thank Lewica for
its discipline and move to the next institutional file; trade unionists and
social-policy organisers hear that the coalition has again purchased calm
with their time. Razem does not need to invent a betrayal line. We have written
it for them, and no later success can rescue this six-month review.

- @poland_event_queue: File the social settlement with the events desk

