on-arrival: government_burden_tenant_seen = 1; news_headline = "Tenant guarantees collide with a coalition mortgage subsidy"

= The coalition can subsidise a home without creating one

Housing Minister **[+ housing_minister +]** of **[+ housing_minister_party +]**
places the coalition draft on the table. KO wants subsidised buyer credit and
faster private construction. PSL's mayors want discretion outside the largest
cities. Banks, developers and young couples with just enough income to borrow
can all imagine themselves in the launch photograph.

Tenant organisations bring a less photogenic warning: money poured into demand
can return as higher prices while deposits, eviction rules and the public
rental stock remain exactly where they were. Lewica has one cabinet meeting to
decide whether tenants enter the bill as its centre, its first instalment—or a
voluntary footnote.

- @tenant_full
- @tenant_first
- @tenant_subsidy

@tenant_full
title: Put tenant guarantees and public homes in the same bill
subtitle: Cost: 2 budget. Delivers the full housing goal and forces KO and PSL to own their resistance.
choose-if: budget >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Full tenant and construction package requires two budget points.
on-arrival: budget -= 2; household_security += 7; local_network += 2; government_delivery += 5; government_goal_housing = 1; ko_relation -= 3; psl_relation -= 2; government_coalition_dissent += 6; fiscal_stress += 2; news_headline = "Tenant guarantees and public construction enter one bill"

**[+ housing_minister +]** leaves with one bill: enforceable tenant guarantees,
municipal land and a public construction fund. Tenant unions can organise
around homes that will exist rather than credits they cannot use. KO warns of
cost and PSL warns of central prescription, but both must now argue against a
visible alternative instead of quietly deleting it in committee.

- @poland_event_queue: File the housing settlement with the events desk

@tenant_first
title: Win the tenant rules now and give municipalities the first sites
subtitle: Cost: 1 budget. Delivers a narrower housing goal the coalition can actually pass.
choose-if: budget >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Enforcement and municipal pilots require one budget point.
on-arrival: budget -= 1; household_security += 4; local_network += 3; public_trust += 2; government_delivery += 3; government_goal_housing = 1; ko_relation += 1; psl_relation += 1; government_coalition_dissent += 2; news_headline = "Tenant guarantees lead a narrower municipal housing bill"

The first bill regulates deposits and eviction procedure, then funds municipal
pilots where land is ready. PSL mayors gain room to prove the model and KO can
claim the programme is bounded. Tenant organisers know the public stock will
remain too small, but they leave with rules that can be enforced and sites on
which the next fight can be built.

- @poland_event_queue: File the housing settlement with the events desk

@tenant_subsidy
title: Pay buyers and ask landlords to volunteer
subtitle: Coalition peace now; the subsidy replaces tenant reform and breaches the six-month record.
on-arrival: budget -= 1 if budget >= 1; household_security += 1; fiscal_stress += 3; ko_relation += 4; psl_relation += 4; government_coalition_dissent -= 4; public_trust -= 1; progressives_dissent += 4; razem_dissent += 6; coalition_blur += 4; government_burden_breached = 1; news_headline = "Buyer subsidies replace binding tenant reform"

Banks can advertise the subsidy before tenant organisations receive the final
text of the voluntary code. Some households cross the mortgage threshold; the
public stock does not grow and no landlord acquires a duty. KO and PSL call the
launch a housing victory. Razem calls it a transfer to prices, and Lewica must
carry that answer into a six-month review it has already breached.

- @poland_event_queue: File the housing settlement with the events desk
